{
  "text": " My brother's girlfriend decided I was trying to humiliate her on purpose, all because of a birthday gift. And the strangest part? She seemed jealous of me because of my brother, even though we're twins. We've loved building LEGO since we were kids. Our family didn't have much money, so every new set was a big event. And even now, at 25, we still give each other LEGO sets. For our birthday, I gave him a huge castle, and he gave me Notre Dame Cathedral. We were both thrilled. His girlfriend got him a gift, too. A beautiful watch. My brother thanked her. He liked it. But he was noticeably more excited about the LEGO. He was already talking about building it the next weekend. A little while later, I got a message from his girlfriend. Apparently, I'd bought an expensive gift on purpose to make her look bad. And I should have warned her in advance that I was planning to give him something expensive. I explained that my brother and I had been exchanging LEGO sets our whole lives, and there was nothing unusual about it. But she kept going. She said LEGO sets were children's toys. She was trying to turn my brother into a grown man, and I was ruining everything. Then she started writing as if I were some kind of rival trying to steal her boyfriend. Let me remind you, I'm his sister. His twin. At first, I didn't even know what to do with that. But a few days later, I went over to help my brother build the castle, and I decided to show him the messages. He took my phone, read them in silence, and suddenly said,",
